s/spec.md\"\nr3=block(kt,\"### Requirement: Knowledge search scans one or all current spaces deterministically within global bounds\",\"### Requirement: Retrieval persists\")\nr3=rep(r3, \"\"\"Search SHALL perform a case-insensitive literal scan over safe UTF-8 Markdown files as they are read from the live targeted spaces. A file whose Knowledge-relative path contains `:` has no unambiguous `kb://` locator, so search SHALL skip it exactly as it skips a non-Markdown file rather than emitting a passage whose locator `read` refuses.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Search SHALL perform a case-insensitive literal scan over safe UTF-8 Markdown files as they are read from the live targeted spaces. A file whose Knowledge-relative path contains `:`, `?`, `#`, or `%` SHALL be searched like any other; its emitted locator SHALL percent-encode exactly those characters in the affected segments and leave every other character literal, so the locator is directly a valid `read` argument.\"\"\")\nr3=rep(r3, \"\"\"#### Scenario: A path with no locator is not searched\n\n- **WHEN** a Space contains a Markdown file whose relative path contains `:`, such as `notes/2026-09-08 14:30 standup.md`\n- **THEN** search returns no passage for it\n- **AND** no result carries a locator that `read` would refuse\"\"\",\n\"\"\"#### Scenario: A path with no locator is not searched\n\n- **WHEN** a Space contains a Markdown file whose relative path contains `:`, such as `notes/2026-09-08 14:30 standup.md`\n- **THEN** search returns its passages with the locator `kb://<id>/notes/2026-09-08 14%3A30 standup.md:<start>-<end>`\n- **AND** passing that locator unchanged to `read` opens the passage; no emitted locator is one `read` refuses\"\"\")\npathlib.Path(\"openspec/changes/kb-locator-recovery/specs/knowledge-tools/spec.md\").write_text(\"## MODIFIED Requirements\\n\\n\"+r3)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\npnpm exec openspec validate kb-locator-recovery --strict 2>&1 | tail -3",
